  @doc ~S"""
  Manage the CEL roles that can be created with this backend.

  `PATCH /v1/auth/jwt/cel/role/{name}`

  ## Arguments

    * `name` — Name of the cel role

  ## Options

    * `:bound_audiences` (array) — Comma-separated list of 'aud' claims that are valid for login; any match is sufficient
    * `:cel_program` (map) — CEL variables and expression defining the program for the role. This is a map with two fields: 1. 'variables', a list of objects with two fields ('name' and 'expression') defining each variable and the exact execution order. 2. 'expression', the final statement to execute and whose result is returned. For example: cel_program = { "variables": [ { "name": "condition", "expression": "len(claims.groups) > 0" }, { "name": "result", "expression": "pb.Auth{Alias: claims.aud, Groups: claims.groups}" } ], "expression": "condition ? result : false" }
    * `:clock_skew_leeway` (seconds) — Duration in seconds of leeway when validating all claims to account for clock skew. Defaults to 60 (1 minute) if set to 0 and can be disabled if set to -1. Defaults to `60000000000`.
    * `:expiration_leeway` (seconds) — Duration in seconds of leeway when validating expiration of a token to account for clock skew. Defaults to 150 (2.5 minutes) if set to 0 and can be disabled if set to -1. Defaults to `150`.
    * `:message` (string) — Static error message if validation fails
    * `:not_before_leeway` (seconds) — Duration in seconds of leeway when validating not before values of a token to account for clock skew. Defaults to 150 (2.5 minutes) if set to 0 and can be disabled if set to -1. Defaults to `150`.
    * `:mount` — where the engine is mounted, `"jwt"` by default.
  """
  @operation "jwt-patch-role"
  @spec patch_role(ExBao.server(), String.t(), keyword()) ::
          ExBao.Operation.result()
  def patch_role(server, name, opts \\ []) do
    ExBao.Operation.call(
      server,
      :patch,
      "auth/#{ExBao.Operation.mount(opts, "jwt")}/cel/role/#{ExBao.Operation.escape(name)}",
      opts,
      body: [
        :bound_audiences,
        :cel_program,
        :clock_skew_leeway,
        :expiration_leeway,
        :message,
        :not_before_leeway
      ],
      content_type: "application/merge-patch+json"
    )
  end

